/-!
# Native open restriction of original global period classes

The literal holomorphic cocycle restricted from the original family
has the same genuine Ext class as the independently constructed cocycle
on the actual restricted family. This is proved with an actual common
refinement and a genuine holomorphic change-of-primitive coboundary.
The original neighborhood comparison therefore preserves these period
classes, and actual nested-open restriction holds for globally defined
coefficients, including the original constant-character classes.

This package does not assert restriction compatibility for coefficients
defined only on an arbitrary intermediate open, nor any local-frame or
generation result. All cohomology groups, scalar maps, and quotient
atlases remain the native original ones.
-/
